{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/278637-totemic-pantheon-wip","id":278637,"title":"Totemic Pantheon (WiP)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-11T23:49:14-07:00","id":278637,"title":"Totemic Pantheon (WiP)","content":"I'm still writing up the founding members, but I've got the Overworld, the Underworld, and the basic premise for them written up, so I decided to post it. I'll be adding the Totems themselves once they're completed.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Totemic Pantheon:</b> Ages ago, mankind once worshiped nature and beasts, but eventually their religious beliefs advanced to more human deities. For thousands of years, the worship of animal spirits was thought to have been lost, but a band of Scions have begun to restore it in the modern age, though they may have deviated from the ancient versions of the legends. This new Totemic Pantheon addresses its members as Totems, or guardian animals. According to the religion they founded, everybody has an animal that represents their true self, and their mortal followers attempt to connect with that spirit animal and live up to its teachings both metaphorically and sometimes literally.<br /> <br /> <br /> This new Totemic Pantheon is definitely unpopular with the other Pantheons that exist, as the human gods and goddesses are loathe to the idea of humans placing mere beasts on the same level of status as they are. The Egyptian deities are more accepting of them given that they tend to have bestial features, themselves, but they still view them as a rival for worshipers and legendary achievements. Another reason why they are hated is because the Totemic Pantheon has no designated culture or ethnicity, it is a melting pot of all cultures, the original founders settling the differences of their racist parents and forming into a unified religion that commingles the bloodlines. Racial ethnicity becomes difficult to identify when you look like a beast, after all. It is quite famous (or infamous) for adopting unclaimed Scions if their parents show no interest in meeting them. But there is also a reason why they are so open to accepting members. The truth is that they are young, and they are new, and in a war against not only the Titans, but the other Pantheons themselves, they need all the help they can get.<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing they are proud to preach about is that they do not believe in eternally punishing their mortal followers for any wrong doings. While they do agree that justice must be paid for their sins, the mortal will not have to worry about facing eternity in torment after their deaths, and all of them will eventually be allowed into the Totemic heaven if they learn to behave themselves. This leniency has done much to sway the mortals to their side, and help to establish their growing power among the population! When the other Pantheons impose merciless punishments for defying their rules, the idea of a more forgiving order of gods and goddesses certainly appeals to those who are susceptible to temptation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Being new to the life of godhood, the Totemic Pantheon is still in development, as its Scions are struggling to achieve divinity in their fight against the Titan Spawn, and against the angry Pantheons who don't like the idea of mortals worshiping beasts again. However, the original founders of this revived Pantheon count 15 in number. They are based on the Fox, the Mole, the Wolf, the Bear, the Rat, the Spider, the Hawk, the Otter, the Snake, the Squirrel, the Horse, the Stag, the Bunny, and the Lion.<br /> <br /> <br /> Among this collection of Totems, the Rat, the Snake, and Spider are the most feared, and worshipers who devote themselves to these Totems usually possess malicious intentions. It is also worth noting that the Totemic Pantheon is chaotic in its social structure. Not only is it a new religion that is still in development, but each Totem has their own idea on how their worshipers should live, which causes their followers to splinter into sub-factions and cults. The wolf Totem, Canis Lupus does his best to establish some form of cohesion among the Totems, and has succeeded in keeping them together as a Pantheon, instead of fracturing into individual deities. Whether they can agree to a unified goal, or if they will forever remain disorganized, however, will be revealed in time.<br /> <br /> <br /> While initially the Totemic Scions may retain their mortal visages, they become progressively more bestial in their features as their power increases. By the time they reach full godhood, a Totem resembles anthropomorphic beasts. These changes are usually cosmetic, however, and do not offer any special benefits without invoking divine powers related to such. Because the deities take on the forms of animals and encourage their worshipers to imitate them, the Totems have been mockingly referred to as the Furry Pantheon. But the Totems are not yet powerful enough to bash the face of every god or goddess who calls them it in public, so they bide their time and build their power until they become worthy of respect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT 1:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> It should be noted that a Scion of the Totems is not required to become a member of the same species as their parent. They are just as likely to become some other creature who shares the same genus, habitat, or dietary traits. It is also entirely possible for them to be completely unrelated, such as Scion of Vixen growing up to resemble the Elephant, or a Scion of Widow becoming a Kangaroo. This allows the Totems to grow in variety, as well as numbers as time passes on!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT 2:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Although they may be new to the ranks of the gods, the Totems have already begun work on constructing Boons and relics to their Scions who wish to join their ranks. One of the most popular boons is the accompaniment of an animal spirit who reflects the beast they feel they most resonate with. The benefits to these animal spirits are two fold. First, the animal spirit functions like a guide and a mentor, leading them on the path towards ascension, and advising them on how to remain in harmony with their inner animal. Secondly, it grants them a stronger affinity towards the animal world, and they find it much easier to advance in the Animal purview. Under the spirit's guidance, they can purchase Animal purview levels at half the normal cost!<br /> <br /> The spirit animal is only a guide and a teacher, however, and does not engage in battle on the Scion's behalf. In fact, the animal spirits make a habit out of fleeing the moment physical danger breaks out, and approach the Scions when they are in an hour of need. Not simply because the Scion asks to be pointed in the right direction. Ascension to godhood isn't supposed to be easy, of course, and the Totems aren't going to hold their hand through the journey.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Overworld:</b> The god realm of the Totemic pantheon is called the Spirit Wylds. Each member of the Pantheon gets their own private habitat designed to be their personal heaven, but nothing prevents them from leaving said habitat and visiting others. Entering another Totem's realm with malicious intent is not looked upon lightly, and more than once the gods have had to convene to settle a dispute between two or more deities who decided to mess with each other and let things get out of hand.<br /> <br /> In the center of the Spirit Wylds lies the Totem Lodge, where all major discussions among the gods and goddesses takes place. It is the place to hold war councils, political debates, trials for crimes against the gods, and discussing strategies on how to increase their power in the mortal world. Strictly speaking, the Spirit Lodge is off limits unless Canis Lupus calls a meeting, and then all able bodied Totems who were invited to the meeting are allowed to enter.<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Underworld:</b> The Totemic underworld is split into three divisions which includes the upper tier called the Wilderness, a middle tier called Widow's Web, and a bottom tier called Widow's Prison. Upon entering the Totemic Underworld, a dead soul is judged by Widow and sent on to either the Wilderness, or they serve a period of time in Widow's Prison as penance for their sins. As a reward, souls who were closely in tuned with their Totem animal in life take on a hybridized form of that animal in the afterlife, much like the gods they worship. While they may gain special abilities based on the structure of their new forms, they are still mortals and do not gain access to the divine abilities of the Totems and their Scions.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Wilderness is where most souls are taken upon being judged by Widow. It is a realm that stretches on seemingly without end, and the majority of it is undeveloped wilderness. The souls of the departed who reside here are allowed to govern themselves (as long as it does not interfere with the Totems or their operations) and form a seemingly infinite number of different societies. These societies are usually dedicated to the teachings and philosophy of the Totems they feel most inspired by, and because there is an unspecified amount of territory to roam, there is little danger of two or more societies clashing with one another. The Wilderness is a place where mortal souls make use of what is around them to create their own paradise. The afterlife is as blissful or tormenting as they make it out to be, so it caters to just about anyone's tastes. The Wilderness offers any climate the inhabitants could ask for, allowing it to be suitable to all species of animals. Depending upon the species, some residents (i.e Carnivores) require meat, which they usually acquire by hunting and feeding on other inhabitants. However, this is a form of the afterlife, so no death is permanent. Those who meet their end here are restored the next day, and the cycle continues. Most (though not all) aren't comfortable with the idea of being hunted down and eaten in what is supposed to be their final resting place, but the deaths are only temporary, so their prey has put up with it so far.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Widow's Web is the border land that separates the Totemic hell from its heavenly counterpart. It is also the gateway that leads both into and out of the Totemic Underworld. Widow's Web is a vast, sprawling network of bridges and tunnel systems caked in webbing, and those wishing to enter or leave the underworld must pass through. If they do not have permission from Widow, the webs will cling to them and ensnare trespassers who do not have the strength or the tools to break free. But if she gives them access, the webs will not hinder them. Those who become ensnared are scooped up by the spidery gate keepers, who whisk them away to Widow for judgement. By default, members of the Totemic pantheon have permission to travel, unless explicitly stated otherwise by Canis Lupus.<br /> <br /> <br /> Widow's Prison is where souls are punished in the afterlife, as well as the tomb in which captured Titan Spawn are confined. The prison is an enormous cavern where inmates are cocooned in spider webs and are either suspended from the ceiling, or sealed to the walls and floors. The prison is guarded by a legion of giant spiders who torment the prisoners by feeding on their bodily fluids and leaving them as mummified husks every day, not unlike Prometheus suffered at the torments of the eagle. The plan is that by leaving the prisoners too atrophied to move, they won't have any chance to escape again! Fortunately for mortals, the Totems do not believe in eternal punishment, though Titan Spawn are an exception. Mortals who are taken here suffer for a period of time that is dictated by Widow, herself, until she feels they have paid their dept. Repeated offenses result in lengthier sentences, but eternal imprisonment is still reserved only for the immortal enemies of the Totems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-14-2014, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T01:47:47-07:00","id":279455,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Members:</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Vixen:</b> Goddess of pleasure and mischief, and is renowned for her sexual addiction and playful trouble making. Vixen's true origins have become a mystery since joining the Totemic Pantheon, but it is heavily implied that she is a child of the Amatsukami. Evidence in her powers, mannerisms, and style of dress suggest that she was conceived by a &quot;fox wife&quot; a mischievous creature who takes the form of a beautiful woman and seduces men into marriage, only to abandon them once their true identity is revealed. Every Scion she has given birth to has been female so far, but she has been known to adopt males if she likes them enough. Her scions are often tricksters, deriving great fun out of playing pranks on mortals and divine alike, though only the more powerful allow themselves to get carried away with their latest mischief.<br /> <br /> Vixen is a sexual icon among the Totems, and her style of dress rarely leaves little to the imagination, accentuating her chest and rear, while exposing arms, legs, face, and midsection as much as possible, her golden hued fur shines like flames in the light and only adds to her enchanting beauty. She is known to be promiscuous and many jokingly attribute her Legend to being entirely constructed in the bedroom. When she enters the battlefield, her weapons of choice are a pair of steel bladed fans, which she uses to fan the flames of her beautiful (yet deadly) fox fire magic. Much like the fox wives of Japan, she has been known to pose as a mortal for long periods of time, even going so far as to marry human males that she has children with. When the child comes of age, Vixen reveals her true identity and their heritage, before abandoning the family, and leaving the child to continue on the path towards ascension.<br /> <br /> When on the mortal world, Vixen's disguises are pretty easy to recognize. She has been a feisty party girl, an erotic dancer, a super model, and even the manager of her own brothel. Anywhere that mortals (particularly men) are likely to enjoy themselves, Vixen will be drawn to it, as her purview dictates.<br /> <br /> Purviews: Sun, Illusion, Fire<br /> <br /> Epics: Manipulation, Appearance<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mole:</b> God of the earth and its valuable minerals. Although there is little evidence to support it, some believe that Mole was a Scion of Hephaestus because of his physical disability. Mole is almost completely blind, only being able to see with the aid of special glasses that have a variety of lens adjustments to point out the details in rare gem deposits and stones he finds in the tunnels beneath the ground. When not wearing these glasses, he is forced to rely on his sense of smell, touch and sound to navigate his surroundings. His scions typically manifest the traits of burrowing creatures, often (though not always) having physical disabilities and impairments brought on by a life time underground.<br /> <br /> Mole is short of stature, being only waist high compared to adult humans, and he is fat in build. His hands and feet appear disproportionately large compared to the rest of his body, with thick claws on the tips that he can use to burrow through the ground. When he's awake, he is almost never seen without wearing a heavy apron, like the kind smelters user in their forges. Because of his stocky appearance, Mole doesn't have much luck when it comes to fathering Scions as most women aren't attracted to him. However, those who do share lineage with him are often blessed with the awesome might of the earth at their command!<br /> <br /> When on the mortal plane, Mole has taken on the disguise of people who work with the earth's resources and have included such professions as iron worker, black smith, miner, gem cutter, and even a glass blower.<br /> <br /> Purviews: Darkness, Earth, Fertility<br /> <br /> Epics: Strength, Wits<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Canis Lupus:</b> The Overgod of the Totems and the one in charge of keeping everyone organized, as much as possible for the Totems. Embodying the wolf, Canis Lupus takes on the role of the pack alpha. He sees the rest of the Totems as his pack, who look to him for leadership and structure in an otherwise chaotic society. Granted not every member of the pantheon shares his views on that matter, but enough respect him to the point where he retains his position. In the society of wolves, the alpha is always the strongest and the bravest. When they begin to show weakness, it usually results in someone in the pack challenging them for leadership. In respect to this, Canis Lupus is renowned as a cunning strategist and exceptional warrior, determined to show his pantheon that he is both strong and smart enough to lead them.<br /> <br /> In appearance, Canis resembles a werewolf standing at nearly 7 feet tall and with muscle tone that shows even through his silvery colored fur. His weapon of choice is the spear, an iconic tool for ancient hunters. He wears trophies from his previous kills to accentuate his past victories, although the types of trophies he wears depends on the prey he is facing. If the prey is weak, simple trinkets are enough to maintain his pride. If the prey is strong, then something more glorious and terrifying is required; perhaps in the form of a skull mask, or a cloak made from the pelt of a fearsome creature.<br /> <br /> When on the mortal plane, Canis Lupus always takes the form of a leader, but prefers a role that also requires him to be strong. The foreman of a construction effort, the commander of a military precision force, the reigning champion of a competitive sporting event, and the ruthless boss of a criminal enterprise when he's in a less noble mood.<br /> <br /> Purviews: Justice, War, Guardian<br /> <br /> Epics: Strength, Intelligence<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ursine:</b> The goddess of strength and self reliance for the Totemic pantheon. Ursine is the bear, a creature renowned for its great size and durability. Some believe that if she wished to, she could challenge Canis Lupus for the position of Overgod, but Ursine does not seem interested in managing the affairs of a whole pantheon, and instead prefers to take care of her own business while leaving the others to theirs. While she is normally docile (as far as deities go), she responds with furious aggression towards anyone who threatens her own safety, or that of something valuable to her, much like a mama bear protecting her cubs. Her ancestry is almost impossible to trace, for she does not speak of who her divine parent was prior to her ascension, and none of the other pantheons have come forth to clarify her lineage. But given that she is a strong, independent female, it is likely that she is descended from the Aesir. Her Scions have no majority towards either male or female, but when others think of her, they tend to imagine daughters being her favored gender.<br /> <br /> Ursine is a hefty woman, standing around 9 feet tall and weighing upwards of 400 lbs in her true form. When in the mortal world, she is still rotund, but is noticeably shorter to blend in with the population. Despite being mistaken for excess fat, much of her weight is comprised of muscle, allowing her to catch fools by surprise when they rile her into a fight. Her species appears to be based on the polar bear, with a pale white shade of fur covering her. When entering battle, her preferred weapon of choice is a pair of weighted gauntlets which are (obviously) far too heavy for any mortal to lift, yet she flings punches as if they were weightless!<br /> <br /> When on the mortal plane, Ursine has taken the disguise of a disgruntled bar tender, a talented chef, a hardened biker, or a woman's weight lifting champion. Typically roles where her large frame and personality are expected, or at least a common enough sight to not raise questions.<br /> <br /> Purviews: Guardian, Frost, Health<br /> <br /> Epics: Strength, Stamina<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rat:</b> God of rebellion and thieves, Rat is quite the unpopular Totem, at least among his fellow divinities. He is a hard ass rebel who prefers to make his own rules, which constantly leads to him getting in trouble with the other Totems. Rat can be found in the shadows, snatching up trinkets that are left in the open, as well as breaking into dwellings and making himself at home, not unlike his mortal counterparts. His Scions often come from the ranks of street gangs, bikers, anarchists, and bad boys.<br /> <br /> In appearance, Rat resembles a punk, his fur being spiked upward and often dyed with bright colors and tattoos. Parts of his fur have bald streaks, revealing a network of scars that he received from his rebellious life style when he pushed someone too far. He wears and assortment of piercings around his ears, nose, lip, eyebrow, and chest, and when he's on the mortal plane, he often dresses in leather, torn clothing, and studded accessories. Whatever disguise he takes on, it is almost always up to trouble, or generally causing people grief. His personal weapon of choice is the knife, preferably ones that are easy to conceal, so he can whip it out to catch his opponents off guard.<br /> <br /> Being the rebel that he is, Rat isn't exactly one for the subtle art of seduction, and uses more direct methods to father his Scions across the world. If he's feeling &quot;gentle&quot; he resorts to using narcotics to leave his partners vulnerable while he has his way with them. If he's in a less romantic mood, he simply forces himself upon them. It is no surprise then, that most of his Scions grow up in an unstable environment, being dumped into a foster home, or facing abuse at the hands of their mortal parent who never wanted them in the first place. This only facilitates their disdain for society, and Rat comes to visit them when he is impressed with their disregard for public safety.<br /> <br /> Purviews: Psychopomp, Chaos, Darkness<br /> <br /> Epics: Dexterity, Perception<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Widow:</b> Goddess of the Underworld for the Totemic pantheon. Widow represents the Spider, and much like Vixen, her lineage is easy to guess at by observing her mannerisms and appearance. Evidence suggests that she is descended from the Greeks, possibly having some form of connection with Arachne. Her version of hell (restraining people and feeding them to animals) is also reminiscent of Prometheus from Greek mythology. Widow governs the afterlife with the aid of a legion of giant spiders who capture trespassers and bring them to her for questioning and sentencing.<br /> <br /> Widow's true form resembles a centaur, having the lower body of an enormous spider, but from the waist up is a more humanoid form, although it has 8 eyes and protruding fangs making it quite hideous to behold! Her weapon of choice is the bow and arrow, the ammunition for which is usually coated in the venom of some of the world's deadliest arachnids! As a spider, Widow has ridiculously acute senses, both from her additional sets of eyes, and her ability to sense vibrations. Truly she is worthy of being the keeper of the Totemic Underworld, for very little escapes her notice.<br /> <br /> The origins of the spiders who roam about her web and prison is a disturbing legend and one which further adds to the terror of Widow. The legend states that when Widow conceives a Sion, she devours her mate shortly after the the deed is done. These giant spiders are the souls of her lovers, continuing to serve their mistress both in death as well as in life, their souls being reincarnated into Widow's private harem of 8 legged servants. Needless to say, not many people like the idea of being enthralled to their own murderer for eternity, so she often uses deceit to lure men into her bedchambers. When in the mortal world, her disguise is usually that of an extraordinarily beautiful woman with a power fetish. She takes great pleasure in watching the men fight among each other for her affections, eager to see which of them will be her lover for the evening, unaware of the fate that awaits those who win her contest.<br /> <br /> Purviews: Prophecy, Death, Mystery<br /> <br /> Epics: Appearance, Perception<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Red Tail:</b> Goddess of the weather and messenger of the Totems. Having the envious power to fly, Red Tail can travel large expanses of terrain more quickly than the land dwelling Totems, which makes her ideal for relaying messages and items. She embodies the Hawk, a swift bird of prey with keen eye sight. That eye sight also helps her navigate the land beneath her, so she knows where to evenly distribute the weather. She is speculated to have been descended from the Egyptian pantheon, but like most of the Totems, she doesn't talk much about her ancestry now that they've founded a new Pantheon.<br /> <br /> When in her true form, Red Tail does not have access to hands as her arms are replaced with a giant set of wings. However, she can use her legs and talons with artistic precision. Her fighting style relies on the use of kicking attacks, while using her wings to remain airborne as well as to distract the enemy with her flourishing movements. In order to reduce wind resistance and make it easier to control her wings, she typically does not wear upper body clothing. When in her human disguises, Red Tail commonly takes the form of someone who is handicapped, particularly focusing on the arms. Not only is this to show she has trouble using her upper limbs for human functions, but it also symbolizes that her wings have been temporarily clipped until she drops her disguise.<br /> <br /> Red Tail is the only member of the founding Totems who has the gift of flight, which brings her both admiration and envy from the rest of the pantheon. Even her Sions display a personality that embraces freedom and wanderlust, which again makes them both admired and envied by their cousins who don't share their gift.<br /> <br /> <br /> Purviews: Fertility, Sky, Psychopomp<br /> <br /> Epics: Perception, Dexterity<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Otter:</b> God of water and the secrets that lie within it. Otter is many things including an explorer, a trickster, a fisherman, and a surfer. In other words, he loves to enjoy life and is very playful in nature, but can be deadly when the situations calls for it. Otter is also highly curious and inquisitive. There are a great many things that dwell beneath the waves, and as the Totem of the seas, he feels compelled to seek them out. This often leads him to clash with Titan Spawn who dwell beneath the waves, causing him to fight them off so they don't venture onto dry land.<br /> <br /> Otter's true form dresses in minimal attire, as too much clothing only provides drag that would slow him down and restrict his movements. There are even legends which state he is a nudist, only donning clothes when he is attending a formal occasion and needs to be polite! His weapon of choice is a two pronged spear that doubles as a fishing tool when he's not skewering his foes in underwater combat!<br /> <br /> Otter's Scions are drawn to adventure with many of them possessing an infamous curiosity streak. Even if they don't hear the call of the sea in their fate, they still feel the urge to travel the land, uncovering hidden mysteries and treasures. When in his mortal disguise, Otter likes to take on the forms of people who satiate his hobbies including sailors, treasure seekers, and water sports athletes. Often his Scions are mothered by women who were seduced by his skills on the water. Otter affectionately refers to them as beach babes, a term he continues to use from his mortal days.<br /> <br /> Purview: Moon, Water, Mystery<br /> <br /> Epics: Appearance, Charisma<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Serpent:</b> God of cruelty and black magic. Serpent is the most hated member of the Totems, having taken on the role of the &quot;adversary&quot; god. When Rat causes trouble, it's because he values his individuality and freedom, but Serpent is evil for the sake of being evil. He takes great delight in causing harm to the other Totems and their Scions completely unprovoked just because it amuses him! When he is confronted with demands to explain himself, he arrogantly replies that a religion is boring without a devil to provide conflict and drama. Serpent is also a known racist, believing that his scaly hide makes him tougher than the soft flesh of some of the other animals he shares power with, and he openly endorses slavery. Given his relation to snakes and his love for causing trouble to mortal and gods alike, he is believed to be descended from the Egyptian pantheon, more than likely with Seht being his father! Serpent has been known to stop his shit and help the other Totems in their fight against the Titan Spawn, but it is more out of a desire to maintain his own grip on power. He can not fend off the whole army of the Titans by himself, and there is doubtfully any other Pantheons who would accept him and his shenanigans, so he recognizes the benefits to keeping his fellow Totems alive... for now!<br /> <br /> In his true form, Serpent resembles a naga, having the upper body of a humanoid reptile, but possesses an enormous (roughly 15 feet long) snake tail instead of legs. His species of snake appears to be the Asp if you were to inspect him, but most people see him appear and know that it's probably best to leave. To Serpent, there is nothing more arousing than the sight of a beautiful woman prostrating her body and soul before him in a sign of total submission. And most of his Scions are conceived by priestesses and worshipers who willingly offer themselves upon his altar in some kind of debauched sex ritual!<br /> <br /> As the god of black magic for the Totemic pantheon, cults dedicated to Scion conduct rituals and ceremonies that would be considered forbidden and illegal in civilized territories. Ritual human sacrifice is just one such way in which they worship him. Because their god promotes slavery, worshipers of Serpent do so as well, and have been known to capture people who become lost in the woods, have their cars break down on the side of the road, or (if they're feeling particularly bold) they simply knock somebody out and toss them in the back of their trunk! In order to prevent their chances of escape, the slaves who prove troublesome are usually sacrificed to Serpent, much to their horror!<br /> <br /> <br /> Purviews: Chaos, Magic, Stars<br /> <br /> <br /> Epics: Manipulation, Stamina<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bushy Tail:</b> Brother of Red Tail and the god of merchantry and business. Bushy Tail embodies the squirrel, and has made it his mission to ensure the Totems have all the supplies they need for the coming war against the Titans. Food, resources, and weapons are what he oversees. If his sister is the messenger of the gods, then Bushy is the store keeper. When questioned how Bushy and Red became two entirely different species upon ascension to godhood, Bushy explains that (like many Scions) they have the same father, but different mothers. They are half siblings, but siblings none the less. He is no more lenient in explaining who his father was than Red Tail is, maintaining the mystery for those wishing to know.<br /> <br /> In his true form, Bushy resembles a spritely fellow who could be mistaken for a teenager. Though his muscles are well toned, they are sleak and graceful, rather than buff and heavy. His tail is as long as he is tall, and is almost as big from the excess fur, appropriately fitting his name. His weapon of choice is the sling, of all things. And he likes to use acorns which he has imbued with Legend for his ammunition. Legends state that these acorns are immensely heavy, to the point beyond human ability to lift them, which makes them suitable weapons against the Titan Spawn when they make impact.<br /> <br /> Bushy and his Scions are known for their acrobatic performances. Like the squirrel in the tree, Bushy is excessively nimble, sprinting along narrow walkways and jumping across gaps to land safely on the other side. Perhaps this is the result of training with his sister, or perhaps it is a symbol of their connection to each other. Whatever the case may be, Bushy Tail could make for a decent substitute if his sister were to ever be incapable of fulfilling her duties.<br /> <br /> Purviews: Fertility, Guardian, Pyschopomp<br /> <br /> Epics: Dexterity, Perception<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Equine:</b> God of athleticism and labors, and is believed to be descended from the Greek pantheon for obvious reasons. Baring the image of the horse, Equine is a symbol of perseverance. Whether it's jumping hurdles, racing track, tilling the land, or hauling loads, horses are strong and hardy beasts, and Equine expects the same of his children. His worshipers are typically farmers, day laborers, or athletes, praying to the horse god to bestow them with the strength and stamina to succeed.<br /> <br /> In his true form, Equine is one of the largest founding members of the Totemic pantheon. Standing at 10 feet tall and with powerfully toned muscles from a life time of hard work, mortals have a tendency to stand in awe when they are close enough to touch him. His fur is light brown with creamy white patches, and he has thick tufts of hair around his shins and forearms. His mane and tail are the same creamy color as the spots that pepper his body. Like Red Tail, he never wears upper body clothing, allowing him full range of motion for working. His mortal disguises have been the farm hand, the star athlete, the quiet construction worker, and cargo loader. Strangely he doesn't take on management positions when in these disguises, but prefers to be one of the workers, likely as a means to impress his &quot;bosses&quot; by showing he can handle any job they assign.<br /> <br /> <br /> Scions of Equine are almost a boon themselves when they join a Band. Their stamina appears limitless, carrying on long after the point where others would stop to rest. There are even legends which tell of a Scion of Equine carrying one or two allies off the battlefield, slumped over their shoulders when a fight takes a turn for the worst. If the Band needs someone to perform a grueling task, chances are a Scion of Equine will step up to answer the call.<br /> <br /> Purviews: Earth, Sun, Health<br /> <br /> Epics: Strength, Stamina<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hart:</b> God of beauty and wisdom. Hart is the stag who rules majestically over the creatures of the forest. He is believed to be descended from the Amatsukami, a belief that is supported by his mannerisms and fighting style. While Canis Lupus does his best to keep the other Totems under control, Hart ironically seems to be taking away his influence with a passive aggressive resistance. Although Hart makes no move to directly oppose Canis, few can deny that the other Totems look to him for guidance when they have run out of ideas. His beauty makes him charismatic, and his oracular powers make him borderline omniscient. He doesn't have to force people to listen to him, they do so of their own free will! The Totems who seek his council the most are Bushy Tail, Red Tail, Mole and Vixen.<br /> <br /> Hart's true form is stunning to behold, and could even seduce humans despite being a beast. His body is sleek and graceful, nimbly bounding over obstacles when moving at high speed, and he moves with the gentle grace of a dancer. From his heart grows a majestic crown of antlers number 12 points. Unlike the other Totems, he has no weapon of choice, instead relying on his own martial prowess if confronted with battle. Hart's disguises in the mortal world have included being a teacher, a wiseman, a shrine priest, a ballet dancer, a martial arts teacher, and a yoga instructor.<br /> <br /> Hart is a pacifist and chooses to avoid battle unless forced into it. When he is forced into it, however, he proves to be an legendary martial artist, striking at his opponent's weak spots, and seeing through their attack patterns with ease. His Scions are blessed (or cursed) with prophecy, able to see into the currents of Fate itself, and warn their companions of its machinations before they happen.<br /> <br /> <br /> Purviews: Fertility, Prophecy, Sun<br /> <br /> Epics: Charisma, Intelligence<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lapin:</b> Former goddess of hearth and home, now she is the goddess of vice and sin. Shortly after the establishment of the Totemic pantheon, Lapin was seduced by Serpent's forked tongue in more ways than one. This caused her to abandon her role as the symbol of family ties and become a debauched hedonist, as well as giving Serpent a constant ally against the gods who despise him. Her addiction to pleasure is even greater than Vixen's, and she is viewed as a symbol of how too much of a good thing is bad for you. She is sometimes referred to as the goddess of excess for the Totemic pantheon, due to her addictive nature. This bunny totem now serves as a constant reminder to the other Totems that if they allow Serpent to wrap his coils too tightly, they too can fall prey to his corrupting influence. In an effort to keep her further under his control, Serpent has trained Lapin in the ways of magic, as a &quot;sign of good faith&quot; according to how he describes it. However, he refrains from teaching her the truly powerful incantations, and instead teaches her how to disrupt the machinations of fate to her own ends. Fortunately, the mind of a goddess is not so easy to dominate, and in one of her final moments of clarity, Lapin created a safety precaution that could one day reverse Serpent's hold over her. Now it is up to her Scions to carry it out, if they can figure out how!<br /> <br /> In her true form, Lapin is quite the beauty, enough to compete with Vixen according to some legends. She has wide hips, both due to her beast form and because she was once a symbol of motherhood. Her fur was once white as snow, but since her corruption, it has now become black as night, save for a patch of white across the left upper portion of her face that covers her left eye and a portion of her forehead. According to the legends, this patch of fur is a symbol of Lapin's safety magic, and proves that she can be redeemed some day and reclaim her former station.Her disguises in the mortal world are usually focused on decadence and sinful pursuits. She has been a cheap whore, a murderer, a drug dealer, a thief and even the manager of a public bath house. Her weapon of choice is the bo-staff, which is perfect for bludgeoning her foes into submission, it also functions as a sexual aid when there are no partners around.<br /> <br /> Scions of Lapin are often cursed by the influence Serpent leaked into their mother. Sexual addiction runs strongly in her bloodline, and the phrase &quot;fuck like rabbits&quot; is used to describe them frequently. Some of these Scions give into their temptations, but there are others who reject Serpent's machinations, and struggle to overcome their curse. Those who succeed, often hope to break the curse entirely, by freeing their mother from his control and restoring her to her former position. Those who struggle against the curse, are far more dedicated to studying Magic than those who submit to it.<br /> <br /> Purviews: Fertility, Health, Magic<br /> <br /> Epics: Appearance, Dexterity<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lion:</b> God of nobility, pride, and honorable combat. Lion's reputation is at odds with Canis Lupus, for while the Wolf Totem takes on the role of being the Overgod, Lion would much rather see himself on the throne, as is befitting the &quot;King of Beasts&quot; that his species is so often called. Lion certainly possesses the charisma and the drive to be a leader, but his biggest weakness is his pride. Lion is too arrogant in his own capabilities to listen to wisdom and common sense, which has allowed Canis Lupus to outsmart his attempts to steal the throne so far. As the god of nobility, Lion sees himself as the bravest and most skilled member of the Totems. As a Hero and even more as a demi god, he was always the most eager to prove his skills in battle, rushing into danger and claiming trophies from his kills to show the mortals how great he was. Now as a full god, Lion views himself as the educated knight among a Pantheon comprised of primitive warriors. Consequently, he is also the least tolerant of Serpent's activities. If he can successfully dispose of the Totemic &quot;devil&quot; where Canis Lupus can not, then surely the other Totems will put him on the throne instead!<br /> <br /> In his true form, Lion appears as a majestic figure. His muscles are strong and well toned, befitting the build of a knight or a general. His mane gleams brightly like the sun, giving him a holy and divine appearance. He also wears golden chainmail that is polished to the point of almost being reflective. Those who are not protected from bright lights are forced to cast their eyes downward to avoid damaging their vision. His disguises on the mortal world have always been positions of lofty status. He has been a military commander, a mega-corporation president, a heavy weight world champion, or a even the leader of his own country, after dethroning the current ruler. His weapon of choice is the broadsword and shield, making him the only founding member of the pantheon who takes up a defensive tool with his weapon!<br /> <br /> Scions of Lion tend to follow in their father's footsteps. They are the bravest of heroes, like the mighty Hercules who faced each of his trials no matter how outlandish they may have been. They often seek to become leader of any Bands they join, and if they are not outright given the position, they will do whatever they can think of to prove they are more worthy of it. Often by outshining the accomplishments of the Band's current leader. Unfortunately their eagerness to please often results in overestimating their own abilities. More than one Scion of Lion has become a martyr, sacrificing their own lives to protect their Band, and failing to ascend to godhood in the process. As a result, those who successfully pass the trials ahead of them are even more worthy of respect and admiration than the ones who failed.<br /> <br /> Purviews: Sun, Justice, War<br /> <br /> Epics: Strength, Appearance</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-10-2014, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T02:23:32-07:00","id":279463,"title":"","content":"So, it looks good, for a pantheon created by Scions. However, I have a suggestion for the gods' purviews. Obviously, they all have Animal, and it does sounds a little redundant. I'm really bad at creating rules, boons and stuff, but I think that it could be the basis for their Pantheon Specific Purview.<br /> Remove the Animal purview from all of them. Instead, make a PSP that would embody the Scion's connection to a spirit figure, an animal mentor. The first boon could also grant the Scion's access to the Animal purview as a reduced cost, and/even without the use of a relic.<br /> <br /> Oh, and by the way, I'll add Guardian to Ursine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T09:21:50-07:00","id":279749,"title":"","content":"I was considering adding that to her in theme with a mother bear protecting its young, but as she's the goddess of self reliance, I instead chose to give her Health, to improve one's chances of survival. I like the idea of changing the animal purview to some kind of boon, as it would allow me to give them a wider variety on their powers and gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T12:20:00-07:00","id":280006,"title":"","content":"There, I went and tweaked the purviews, changed Animal to something else they might be in control over, and I added an explanation for the existence of a Spirit Animal in the previous post.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T03:58:57-07:00","id":280814,"title":"","content":"Looking at the whole list of gods, I think you could add another one, an herbivore. A horse or a bull could be good, but I'd prefer if it was a Stag. He could be a strong rival to Canis Lupus, trying to reign through sheer majesty, contrasting the wolf's rule of &quot;terror&quot;. I'd give him Epic Charisma, maybe Appearance or Intelligence, and also Fertility as a Purview.<br /> <br /> Also : why are you limiting your gods to 3 purviews and 2 Epics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T05:16:57-07:00","id":280892,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the predator/prey concept seems missing here.<br /> The &quot;Horned God&quot; may not have been originally human. And speaking of which, there are distinctions between the horned and the antlered, so there could be a unifying figure.<br /> <br /> And no &quot;feline&quot; figure?<br /> *cries*<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T10:13:14-07:00","id":281220,"title":"","content":"When doing research on the game, I thought I came across something that stated characters had the 3-2 set up. Maybe it's different for full gods than it is scions; what do you suggest would be a good number for them?<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, I'm also sad I didn't add in a feline. I like cats!<br /> <br /> <br /> I also didn't notice the lack of plant eaters when I was writing this up, but now that you mention it, it could use some less violent members among its ranks. I'll add those in when I finish writing them up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Also, I just now noticed that I completely forgot to put in Squirrel!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-14-2014, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T10:29:20-07:00","id":281232,"title":"","content":"Hm, there's no canon limit on the number of purviews and attributes that can be associated with a god. It's actually kinda random, and it depends on what makes the more sense according to the god's history. For instance, Geb has 5 Purviews, but no Epic, while Aphrodite is all about the attributes. And then we have gods like Odin, who has 6 attributes and 7 purviews, discounting the PSP. So...as long as it fits thematically, yeah, you can put whatever powers you want. Unless you want something more balanced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T11:07:25-07:00","id":281284,"title":"","content":"Ah, good. I was afraid I messed something up. The reason I gave them 3 Purviews was because I felt 3 was enough to qualify for what they are the rulers over. It felt kind of difficult to explain why Canis Lupus would have domain over the sun, moon, and star. I decided to give Moon to Otter, since it has a connection with the sea, and Stars to Serpent, as they are often associated with mysticism.<br /> <br /> <br /> On another note, Hawk and Squirrel are going to be siblings. Red Tail and Bushy Tail respectively. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T19:42:36-07:00","id":281830,"title":"","content":"There we go. It took longer than I would have liked because right after my previous post, we lost internet until just now. I added Squirrel (like he was supposed to be), along with Horse, Stag, Rabbit, and Lion. Bringing the pantheon founders up to 15 instead of 10. What do you guys think about them?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I'm starting work on a description of each of their signature weapons, particularly the legendary versions they each use. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T05:02:43-07:00","id":282176,"title":"","content":"The writing is neat, but 15 gods is a lot, compared to the canon ones (although, if you include Ragnarok, the Aesir have 17 members). I also noticed that while many of them have Epic Appearance, only one of them has Epic Wits. Again, you don't need to make it balanced : only 4 of the core pantheons have someone with the fire purview, for instance.<br /> <br /> And why do you want to give them weapons? They're animals, some of them should only fight with their fangs and claws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T07:57:37-07:00","id":282303,"title":"","content":"Well yes, they are, but they didn't start off that way. They began their journey as Scions to the pre-existing pantheons and then left to form their own. So some of these tools were given to them as a reward during their ascension (and are thus tied with their Legend), and others serve as a badge of office for their new station. Canis Lupus' spear is called the Scepter of the Great Hunt, for example. Besides, if every Totem relied on their body to fight, I imagine it would get kind of disappointing for their scions.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;I want to be a Totem, what kind of weapons can I expect?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Congratulations, you get to punch things, all across the board!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> And not all of them have weapons. Mole and Hart, for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for 15 being a lot. That's probably true for the game mechanics, but if I'm not mistaken, the Greeks went pretty nuts with the size of their actual pantheon. They seemed to have a god for <i>everything</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> I tried to make at least 1 Totem for each of the available Purviews (excluding the pantheon specific ones, of course) and I tried to choose attributes that would be appropriate for their station. Wits for Mole, I felt was necessary to survive the dangers of living underground, such as collapsed tunnels, locating food, inspecting resources, and keeping his barrings straight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-15-2014, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T09:39:02-07:00","id":282395,"title":"","content":"Actually, there was only twelve olympians gods. Thirteen, if you count Hestia who decided to leave Olympus to make some room for Dionysus. There are other gods (Thanatos, Nyx, Hypnos, Iris...), but they weren't considered part of the &quot;main&quot; gods.<br /> <br /> And many gods don't have weapons. If their kids want to fight, well, they can always ask the closest blacksmith god they can find! Take Aphrodite, Hera or once again, Dionysus. And usually, the gods who have one doesn't lend them to their children. I don't think I ever saw a Scion game with Thor giving Mjollnir away. A piece of it, yes, but not the whole weapon.<br /> <br /> On another note, do you intend to give your gods Associated abilities?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T09:48:25-07:00","id":282407,"title":"","content":"Hmm, maybe you're right. Besides, I doubt I know enough about how to create balanced weapons for the setting. Leaving them as simply &quot;weapons of choice&quot; is easier. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> As for their abilities, I'm not sure yet. It may take some more planning to map them out effectively.<br /> <br /> <br /> On a side note, I had an idea. If a piece of that gun was made from Mjolnir, would that mean only the worthy could lift it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T09:59:19-07:00","id":282417,"title":"","content":"Well, one of the pre-gen Scion from the core book <i>has</i> a gun with a piece of Mjollnir in it. I guess that makes him worthy enough? (Besides, the only other person who could lift the hammer was Thor's oldest son, Magni. So I'd say it runs in the blood?)<br /> <br /> If you want your weapons, you could always create some relics, along with guides and creature. They'd give an idea of what gifts these Totems can grant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T13:41:57-07:00","id":282657,"title":"","content":"Would be a hell of a birthright getting to wield the hammer itself some day. Maybe during Ragnarok when Thor is supposed to die? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T23:38:18-07:00","id":283512,"title":"","content":"Crap, I think I'm starting to get inspired to go on a fan-content spree again like I did in the WoD forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T13:37:38-07:00","id":284147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/278637-totemic-pantheon-wip?p=282417#post282417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, one of the pre-gen Scion from the core book <i>has</i> a gun with a piece of Mjollnir in it. I guess that makes him worthy enough? (Besides, the only other person who could lift the hammer was Thor's oldest son, Magni. So I'd say it runs in the blood?)<br /> <br /> If you want your weapons, you could always create some relics, along with guides and creature. They'd give an idea of what gifts these Totems can grant.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the book &quot;Drinking Midnight Wine&quot;, one character is Thor's umpteenth great-grandson and somehow inherited Mjonlnir. Only the poor hammer is so old and senile that it sometimes forgets to come back and just keeps blasting through things until it forgets why it's doing that, then just falls to the ground...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T14:43:10-07:00","id":284226,"title":"","content":"I'm considering a converting the Great Evils from Diablo into a pantheon for Scion. Would anybody be interested in seeing that? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Basically put, you'd be the child of a lord of hell, and during the course of your ascension, you'd claw your way up the ranks, outsmarting and overpowering your siblings for the right to hold a throne of your own!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-16-2014, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T20:19:38-07:00","id":284549,"title":"","content":"Well at least somebody liked my idea. Anyone else? I've already got them written up, just tweaking the ideas a bit as I think of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T10:54:45-07:00","id":285148,"title":"","content":"<b>Story Ideas</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Hero:</b> By whatever means it happened, you became awakened to the spiritual world, and learned you were conceived by a Totem. But your spirit is out of balance, and you have strayed too far from the natural world. They have sent you a guide to lead you on the proper path, and to even greater rewards, should you stay the course. Maybe you'll follow in the footsteps of your parent. Maybe you'll carve your own path towards spirituality. The choice is up to you, and you're spirit guide will show you the way towards your destiny.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Demi God:</b> Something has happened, the spirit world is in chaos... more so than usual. The Totems are gone and nature has no guardians to lead it. Then you find out why, the gods and goddesses of the human pantheons have abducted the Totems and locked them in cages like wild beasts. Without Widow to grant permission, souls can not travel through Widow's Web, and are trapped in her webs, awaiting judgement in the realm between heaven and hell. Even Serpent wasn't able to escape their prejudice, much to your amusement! This blatant disrespect can not be tolerated, but you know the consequences of challenging a full god in your current state. So it's time to stage a jail break, instead!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>God:</b> The Totems are free and now they count you among their number. No longer are you a wandering shaman or a vision quester, you are one with the animal pantheon. Will you forgive the other gods for their disrespect and focus on the Titans, or will you show them what wild animals do when you intrude upon their lair?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ragnarok:</b> Set into the distant future, mankind has grown callous and arrogant. Having been pushed to desperation by the Titans and the warring gods, they seek to create more effective weapons and defenses. Of course no man made weapon is going to put a dent in the Gods, but that doesn't stop them from polluting the earth and torturing animals in their attempts to prove otherwise. The Totems feel the spirit world crying out for mercy, and they know it's pain for it is mirrored within them. As their habitats are destroyed and their animals slaughtered, the Totems feel their power dwindling a little more. Nature is losing its power in the face of military expansion, and the Totems which govern it are gradually dying. If the Totemic Pantheon can not restore the balance of nature and heal the land, they will die, and so will the spirit world with it. These are the End Times!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-17-2014, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T18:50:55-07:00","id":288130,"title":"","content":"I'm curious, what are their Virtues? Any example Birthrights?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T23:16:59-07:00","id":288372,"title":"","content":"The animal spirit guide was one possible birthright. Recently, I started to think of a possible exclusive Purview for members of this pantheon. Maybe something having to do with Totems, such as repelling enemies or receiving blessings in the form of animal carvings and war paint. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> As for their Virtues, I'm trying to think of what would be appropriate for a pantheon that symbolizes connection to nature and spirits of the wild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T02:49:59-07:00","id":288434,"title":"","content":"Well, Harmony is a given. Loyalty to your pack, maybe? And I think I'd say Valor and Endurance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T18:14:07-07:00","id":295470,"title":"","content":"The topic of this thread reminded me of two things:<br /> <br /> 1. It reminds me of the Celestial thread, where people are making a pantheon based on the spirits of Werewolf:The Apocalypse, which uses a similar method of totem hierarchy on a smaller scale.<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> 2. It reminded me of the Spirit Nation thread that I did, which train-wrecked so hard that it caused global nuclear fallout, destroyed the Earth, disproved the existence of gods, and bombed the game universe so hard that it rebooted in Safe Mode.<br /> <br /> On another note, Damballah from the First Edition Loa would've loved this pantheon, especially the Serpent, being that he loved being in his snake form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T04:52:17-07:00","id":295715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/278637-totemic-pantheon-wip?p=295470#post295470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. It reminded me of the Spirit Nation thread that I did, which train-wrecked so hard that it caused global nuclear fallout, destroyed the Earth, disproved the existence of gods, and bombed the game universe so hard that it rebooted in Safe Mode.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously? You come to this thread, a thread from someone who's new to Scion, to complain about how a past thread of yours has been badly received? I don't want to take a side on the Spirit Nation debate, but...let it go, you're really not helping your case right now.<br /> Also, the main difference between your two works is that Nyrufa's not basing his pantheon on a real population. His totems are all Scions who ascended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T13:41:46-07:00","id":297450,"title":"","content":"Here's what I got so far. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Shamanism:</b> In the old religions, people who claimed to have a connection with the spirit world and could communicate with it were called Shamans. The power of Shamanism is the Pantheon specific Purview for the Totemic Pantheons. By using artistic depictions of spirits, the user is able to perform various spells and rituals. Sometimes these depictions are in the form of carved statues and figurines. Other time, they take the form of ritual tattoos and body paint. Whatever the case may be, a user of Shamanism is never truly alone, so long as the spirits are there to answer his or her call.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Level 1 - Totem Figurine:</b> The user carves an animal statue that is small enough to fit in someone's palm. Anyone who is in physical possession of the figurine gains +1 to an epic attribute that would be associated with that animal. Such as Epic Strength for a bear, or Epic Dexterity for a rabbit. Although a person can own multiple figurines, they can only gain a benefit once from each animal. So carving 5 bear figurines is just a waste if you plan to use them all yourself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Level 2 -</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Level 3 - Spiritual Absorption:</b> This somewhat gross boon allows the user to gain bestial talent in various skills by consuming an associated body part of an animal. Eating the legs of a rabbit might allow them to run faster or jump higher, consuming the ears of a dog may improve their audio capacity, or eating the claws of a cat may give them unusually sharp fingernails. The effects to Spiritual Absorption last for 24 hours, at which point, they must consume the body part again to renew it's effects. Also... the body parts must be eaten raw...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Level 4</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Level 5 - Vision Quest:</b> The user of this boon gains the ability to partially enter the spirit world. Their body remains in a trance-like state in the physical world, but their mind and spirit travel in another plane of existence. At the completion of a Vision Quest, the shaman often receives a prophetic warning of things to come. Novice Vision Questers who are not used to the way spirits communicate may be confused by what the visions mean, but those with the wisdom and experience of multiple visits are better skilled at deciphering them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Level 6 - Totem Pole:</b> This boon allows the user to carve a large totem that bares the image of 4 different animal gods or goddesses. It is a more powerful version of Totem Figurine in the sense that it provides it's gifts across a wide area, and not just to whoever is touching it at the time. Totem Pole gives a +1 to an Epic Attribute associated with each of the animals it depicts. It's effective range is 1 mile equal to the amount of Legend used to create it, and it only benefits those who the creator acknowledges as allies. Unfortunately, the Totem Pole must be recharged once a month in order to maintain it's benefits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Level 7 -</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Level 8 - Tattoo Conjuring:</b> With this boon, the Shaman has the ability to use their own body as a summoning catalyst for various animals. By spending Legend, they can transform a tattoo into a real animal, which will separate from their body and obey their will to the best of it's ability. When the power is disabled, the animal once again merges with the user and becomes a regular tattoo again. The user can only animate tattoos based on animals in this manner, and the animal will be life size while it is seperated. Because there is a limited amount of space on someone's body, the user should be careful about choosing which animals they want at their disposal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Level 9 -</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Level 10 - Spirit Manifestation:</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T14:37:35-07:00","id":297514,"title":"","content":"Interesting idea. Might want to be careful with Spiritual Absorption, which has a power identical to a similarly ranked Animal boon. Also, borrowing from Gotham By Night's Anunna and their PSP, called Me, maybe a power that allows the Scion to act as a Relic for a specific Animal purview for himself and those touching him/her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T09:59:56-07:00","id":299028,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>General Relationships:</b> The Totemic Pantheon has an interesting relationship with the world. At first glance, many would tell you the world is chaotic and unpredictable. That only the fittest survive in the wilds, and while this may be true, it is not all that the Totems represent. They find harmony in the natural order of things. The food chain is a form of social hierarchy, with some animals working together to keep the world in balance. Destruction is a necessary act, for with its passing comes the chance for new things to grow and evolve. By facing destruction, the next generation can learn to adapt and survive until the next tragedy befalls them and the cycle continues.<br /> <br /> It is difficult for outsiders to comprehend this philosophy, seeing a pantheon that espouses chaos while at the same time warring against the Titan of Chaos itself. The Totems claim that unrestrained chaos only brings destruction, causing the ecosystem to be thrown out of balance. Unbalanced food ratio causes starvation or possibly over eating, over population causes one species to grow too powerful, and environmental disasters kill thousands. If the chaos is skillfully orchestrated, the Totems believe it can benefit those who live within it. If the chaos runs rampant, it will only bring the doom of those affected by it.<br /> <br /> While Canis Lupus has amassed the power needed to impose a form of society among the other Totems, his rule as Overgod is shaky at best. Much like the animal kingdom, the Totems are prone to infighting and preying upon one another for their own gain. The fact that Hart is another Totem who has garnered respect among his peers, while both Lion and Serpent have plans to steal the throne indicates that Canis has several other candidates who might replace him if he lets things fall to pieces.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Totemic Pantheon is unpopular with many of the other Pantheons of earth. While there are many gods and goddesses who have taken the form of animals in the past, they have chosen to live by human ways, and these transformations were only temporary. The Totems, however, choose to live by the ways of animals, living in paradoxical harmony with nature, and this offends their fellow deities. What sort of divine being would cast aside his manhood to live in a cave eating raw deer carcasses? Scions who are raised in human society and voluntarily choose to join such a life style are also looked upon with disdain by those who feel themselves more civilized and respectable.<br /> <br /> <br /> Living as beasts and following the laws of nature over civility, the Totems can be mistaken as disrespectful and savage. They do not recognize human laws or customs, only those of the spirit world. And this has lead to violence and rebellion when they encounter humans that refuse to properly respect the ways of nature. These outbursts are especially dangerous when they encounters beings of similar power who support humanity's disrespect. In fact, there have been cases in which the other Pantheons view the Totems as a threat to thousands of years of progress. In their eyes, if they allowed humans to go back to worshiping the beasts of the land, it could result in devolving society back to the stone age, and that simply will not do.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are times when the Totems have blended into human society before, such as when they are looking to produce Scions. Only the more perverted or fanatical cults are willing to mate with animals directly. Most would prefer a human lover at the time, and so the Totems adopt human disguises. Considering sexual activity to be perfectly natural, they are far lest modest about such things, and have trouble understanding why humans are so sensitive about the subject. They have also used their disguises as a means of keeping a watch over the human population. By doing so, they can monitor whether or not they are posing a threat to the spirits, and hopefully move to stop it before it goes too far. Regardless, they still feel most comfortable in the wilds, and spend most of their time in animal form.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Totems are not mindless animals, however. Even the pantheon's founders were born and raised human. They did not decide to become animals completely. They embody the spirituality of what that animal represents, but they still retain their sentient minds. This has caused many foes in the past to underestimate them, being caught by surprise when what they think are wild beasts demonstrate keen insight and strategy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Scions of the Pantheon can expect two kinds of discrimination depending on their origins. Those who are natively born into the pantheon, can expect to be treated like animals by the more prejudice oriented Scions. Those who are adopted into the pantheon can expect other forms of ridicule, with such comments like &quot;Were you raised by wolves!?&quot; to be a common response to their actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> The beast headed gods of Egypt have found an accord with the Totems, however, and are perhaps the only Pantheon the Totems can reliably call an ally. While their Egyptian counterparts are not as focused on their animal characteristics, they do have a close enough relation to animals that they don't feel complete disdain for the Totems.<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Scion Relationships:</b> During their visitation, most Scions find that their parent is rather alien and difficult to comprehend. As spiritual beings, they are removed from the limits of physical and scientific understanding. During their Hero years, many Scions of this pantheon have been known to struggle with understanding the will of the gods as they try to find the correct path towards spiritual harmony. In an effort to gain a deeper level of understanding, Totem Heroes are driven to commune with the wilds, partaking in ceremonies and rituals that strengthen one's connection to the spirit world. Once they obtain the ability, they may also spend extended periods of time on a Vision Quest, learning to decipher the meaning behind the Totem's cryptic messages.<br /> <br /> As they later progress to Demi Gods, they find their parents are easier to understand. They now have a firm concept of what it means to be a spiritual entity, and following the proper path is easier to recognize. They are also more in touch with their inner beast and see the world with a less human perspective and clouded judgement. Now that they have learned how to understand the spirit world, they turn their focus to harmonizing with their animal. Demi God is the stage where most Scions of this pantheon start to lose touch with human society.<br /> <br /> Upon finally ascending to godhood, the Scions of the Totems achieve a state of enlightenment. Now as fully spiritual beings, they are freed of the restrictive preconceptions of humanity and the physical world. But with this enlightenment also comes its own share of problems, for now that they are detached from human civilization, they find associating with it to be more difficult. Additionally, their parent's enemies now turn their attention on them, considering them as potential rivals or possibly allies they can turn against their parent. Ascending into the ranks of the Totems thrusts the Scion into the chaotic power plays and infighting of the pantheon.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Scion of the Totems can choose to follow in their parent's foot steps, adhering to their teachings and philosophy. Doing so often causes the Scion to take on the traits of a species related to their parent. However, if the Scion has the will to follow their own path to ascension, they have been known to take on the characteristics of completely different animals. Doing this broadens the ranks of what the Pantheon has to offer, but adding a new animal spirit is considered to be a difficult quest, for it includes forming their own philosophy and guidelines in which to follow. Without a parent to guide them, Scions who choose this path often take longer to reach godhood than one who follows another's example.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> When it comes to parenting, Serpent is easily the worst out of the Totems. As the god of cruelty and black magic, his Scions are known to exhibit signs of racism, sadism, blood lust, sexism, power hungry, and dementia. They often develop the features of various reptiles including snakes and lizards. Scions who choose to shun their dark father and seek a more noble invoke the wrath of Serpent who considers them unworthy of his blood. Not only this, but the other Totems and their children view them as evil and untrustworthy simply for carrying the dark essence of Serpent within them. During their mortal years, Serpent plans and schemes different ways in which to make his rebellious offspring fall. Those who die in their quests are claimed by Serpent in the afterlife as slaves, where they are tormented by his more loyal followers, as a constant warning to any other Scions who would dare refuse his teachings. Those who manage to succeed in reaching godhood, however, are considered to be purified of Serpent's tainted essence, and they have every reason to hate the snake god. Serpent is usually furious that not only has one of his children escaped his grasp, but they have now been added to his ever growing list of enemies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Mortal Relationships:</b> Only the cults dedicated to worshiping the Totems appear to have the wisdom necessary to comprehend their actions. The worship ceremonies they conduct harken back to the days of tribal rituals and involve the use of body paint, masks, frantic dancing, partaking of drugs, a great hunt, or offering sacrifices. Totems visit their worshipers in the forms of animals, man-beasts, or even human form wearing the pelt of the animal they represent.<br /> <br /> The priests of their cults bare the title of Shaman, and are recognized as those who have a deep connection to the spirit world. In the Totemic religion, nobody can just decide to become a Shaman. Instead, the Totems hand pick their priests, visiting them in their dreams and communicating their desires, which the Shaman then passes along to their cult.<br /> <br /> Siring within their cult is the easiest way for a Totem to produce a Scion. Their followers consider any such child to have the potential to become a powerful Shaman, and this belief is reinforced by the Scion manifesting their divine powers. These cults have been known to offer up virgins of either sex in a mating ritual, with the hopes that their Totem will see fit to bless them with such a child. However, while their cults may be the easiest way, it is not the only way they seek.<br /> <br /> If the mortal world proves to be overstepping its bounds, the Totems have been known to breed with the more civilized portion of society. They do this because they hope that by raising the child in human dominated society, they can become an arbiter for both realms, and figure out a way to solve the problem that doesn't result in open warfare. Sadly, being raised by humans means they grow addicted to human comforts, and their ability to view the spiritual side of the argument is diminished from those raised within the cult.<br /> <br /> <br /> The largest collection of Totem worshipers belong to tribal communities. In the west, this includes the ranks of the Native American tribes. However, while they are the more traditional cultists, they are not their only source of worship. Traveling hippies and reclusive druids have also been known to pay homage to the Totem spirits, as do medicine men and crystal healers. Overall, anyone who feels a deep connection to the land and its creatures can potentially be a Totem worshiper.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T00:50:15-08:00","id":304264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/278637-totemic-pantheon-wip?p=295715#post295715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seriously? You come to this thread, a thread from someone who's new to Scion, to complain about how a past thread of yours has been badly received? I don't want to take a side on the Spirit Nation debate, but...let it go, you're really not helping your case right now.<br /> Also, the main difference between your two works is that Nyrufa's not basing his pantheon on a real population. His totems are all Scions who ascended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, there may be a chance that someone would see &quot;Totem&quot; and immediately think &quot;Indian&quot;, given what Westerns and other books have stated about the Native Americans. Basically, the difference that we had on that thread is whether to completely categorize each and every pantheon in Native American society (something that would satisfy the culture, but completely be dismissed by those that can find it overwhelming), or whether to simplify the pantheons into a single pantheon (something that would've satisfied most casual players, but would anger people who've stated that the simplified version was &quot;racist&quot; Tell me that when you read the first edition of Werewolf: The Apocalypse, that you didn't think that the spirit mechanics reminded you of Indians in Western schlock.<br /> <br /> That was the thought that I had when I first saw this thread. I don't have any opinion, whatsoever, on how the OP should do his pantheon. I just saw the similarities when I saw the word &quot;Totemic&quot;. That's all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:45:12-08:00","id":304914,"title":"","content":"Well taking into account that I have zero knowledge about the native American language and almost just as much on their culture, I don't think it would have been anywhere near accurate enough. I would probably have including things like smoking peace pipes and doing rain dances, which would come across as heavily enforcing stereotypes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> I decided to go more with the aspect of animal spirits, and how these spirits resonate with a person's identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T23:32:39-08:00","id":305359,"title":"","content":"While Nyrufa's fictional Pantheons aren't my cup of tea, they're not offensive racist stereotypes of anything. There's tons of cultures, all over the world, with totemic animal figures. It may, in fact, be the single oldest form of religion. There are some suggestions that even as far back as Neanderthals, there were bear cults and attempts to draw power from totem beasts. <br /> <br /> My deal with this Pantheon is that each and every member needs Animal, and why would you play a member of this Pantheon <i>without</i> taking Animal.. their whole identity revolves around Animal... so their PSP is going to either <i>be</i> Animal, or be a very, very closely related thing that ends up kinda toe-stepping all <i>over</i> Animal. The suggested PSP of &quot;Shamanism&quot; is already basically copying existing Animal Boons. That's a challenge to overcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-07T06:18:42-08:00","id":305618,"title":"","content":"Nyrufa's system potentially can have many beings of power that owe no allegiance to any pantheon.<br /> And in a way there's something that makes sense. Anything that gave an edge to a person when it came to keeping the mind, body and soul whole, which typically revolved around acquiring the basics in life, a person will see that one &quot;thing&quot; as a personal symbol, or &quot;totem.&quot;<br /> Apex predators were/are usually looked upon because they can hunt for food, sleep where they will most of the time, and have little to worry about when it comes to &quot;lesser&quot; species. In today's timeframe, simply being noticeable can be a danger. So the bum on the street might identify more with the humble mouse.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T14:19:23-08:00","id":306915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/278637-totemic-pantheon-wip?p=305359#post305359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While Nyrufa's fictional Pantheons aren't my cup of tea, they're not offensive racist stereotypes of anything. There's tons of cultures, all over the world, with totemic animal figures. It may, in fact, be the single oldest form of religion. There are some suggestions that even as far back as Neanderthals, there were bear cults and attempts to draw power from totem beasts.<br /> <br /> My deal with this Pantheon is that each and every member needs Animal, and why would you play a member of this Pantheon <i>without</i> taking Animal.. their whole identity revolves around Animal... so their PSP is going to either <i>be</i> Animal, or be a very, very closely related thing that ends up kinda toe-stepping all <i>over</i> Animal. The suggested PSP of &quot;Shamanism&quot; is already basically copying existing Animal Boons. That's a challenge to overcome.</div> </div> </div> </div>They used to all have animal, but then I went back and changed it. Instead of being forced to choose it, they now have a guide as a standard gift / birthright. Also, they represent the spiritual side of the animal world, instead of it's more physical aspects. What do people think about when it comes to wolves? Strong, loyal, works well with others, brave. You can be a child of the wolf, without having a pack of canines following you all over the place.<br /> <br /> That's why their PSP involves using artwork such as carvings and paintings to draw power. The artistic depiction symbolizes what the pantheon is about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}